      "@id": "foaf:name"
    },
    "github": {
      "@id": "bopv:github"
    },
    "_comment_structure": "Where a BOP concept has an AOP-ontology counterpart it reuses that term, because the two frameworks share a grammar and should be queryable together. No term is minted for the beneficial direction: that is carried by the PATO action on the event.",
    "events": {
      "@id": "aopo:has_key_event",
      "@container": "@set"
    },
    "relationships": {
      "@id": "aopo:has_key_event_relationship",
      "@container": "@set"
    },
    "event": {
      "@id": "aopo:has_key_event",
      "@type": "@id"
    },
    "relationship": {
      "@id": "aopo:has_key_event_relationship",
      "@type": "@id"
    },
    "upstream_event": {
      "@id": "aopo:has_upstream_key_event",
      "@type": "@id"
    },
    "downstream_event": {
      "@id": "aopo:has_downstream_key_event",
      "@type": "@id"
    },
    "role": {
      "@id": "bopv:role",
      "@type": "@vocab"
    },
    "position": {
      "@id": "bopv:position",
      "@type": "xsd:integer"
    },
    "adjacency": {
      "@id": "bopv:adjacency",
      "@type": "@vocab"
    },
    "biological_level": {
      "@id": "ncit:C25664"
    },
    "_comment_bioevent": "AOP-Wiki RDF does not put the triple on the key event directly: it hangs an aopo:BiologicalEvent node off aopo:hasBiologicalEvent carrying obo:GO_0008150 (process), obo:PATO_0001241 (object) and obo:PATO_0000001 (action). BOP-Hub keeps the flat form, so these three are not join-compatible with AOP-Wiki as they stand; reshaping to a bioevent node is a content change, not a context change.",
    "process": {
      "@id": "aopo:has_process",
      "@type": "@id"
    },
    "object": {
      "@id": "aopo:has_object",
      "@type": "@id"
    },
    "action": {
      "@id": "aopo:has_action",
      "@type": "@id"
    },
    "measurement_methods": {
      "@id": "obo:MMO_0000000",
      "@container": "@set"
    },
    "_comment_evidence": "The three modified-Bradford-Hill dimensions reuse the predicates AOP-Wiki RDF carries on a KER (ncit:C80263, edam:data_2042, edam:operation_3799), and essentiality reuses ncit:C48192 from an AOP. AOP-Wiki's values are free prose; BOP-Hub's are graded concepts from bopv, so the predicate is shared and the value space is not. confidence has no AOP-Wiki counterpart and is minted.",
    "evidence": {
      "@id": "bopv:evidence"
    },
    "biological_plausibility": {
      "@id": "ncit:C80263",
      "@type": "@vocab"
    },
    "empirical_support": {
      "@id": "edam:data_2042",
      "@type": "@vocab"
    },
    "quantitative_understanding": {
      "@id": "edam:operation_3799",
      "@type": "@vocab"
    },
    "essentiality": {
      "@id": "ncit:C48192",
      "@type": "@vocab"
    },
    "confidence": {
      "@id": "bopv:confidence",
      "@type": "@vocab"
    },
    "overall_confidence": {
      "@id": "bopv:overallConfidence",
      "@type": "@vocab"
    },
    "_comment_applicability": "taxa, sex and life_stage use the predicates AOP-Wiki RDF actually uses (ncbitaxon:131567 with 4,035 uses, obo:PATO_0000047 with 1,622, aopo:LifeStageContext with 1,680, in release 2026.11.21). An earlier version of this context mapped taxa to aopo:TaxonomicApplicability, which appears zero times in AOP-Wiki RDF, so the join it existed for could never have matched. interventions, diseases and phenotypes have no AOP-Wiki counterpart -- AOP-Wiki carries domain of applicability as free text in aopo:AopContext -- so they are minted.",
    "taxa": {
      "@id": "ncbitaxon:131567",
      "@type": "@id",
      "@container": "@set"
    },
    "sex": {
      "@id": "obo:PATO_0000047",
      "@type": "@id",
      "@container": "@set"
    },
    "life_stage": {
      "@id": "aopo:LifeStageContext",
      "@type": "@id",
      "@container": "@set"
    },
    "interventions": {
      "@id": "bopv:intervention",
      "@type": "@id",
      "@container": "@set"
    },
    "diseases": {
      "@id": "bopv:disease",
      "@type": "@id",
      "@container": "@set"
    },
    "phenotypes": {
      "@id": "bopv:phenotype",
      "@type": "@id",
      "@container": "@set"
    },
    "modulating_factors": {
      "@id": "bopv:modulatingFactor",
      "@container": "@set"
    },
    "factor": {
